<StanceStatePage state="fl">
  <p>This webpage houses the responses to 6 questions
    crafted by the Florida Stance on Science team. Every question was sent to candidates
    in both English and Spanish.</p>
    <p>Only official candidates who will appear on ballots were contacted.</p>
    <p>Candidates were contacted in July 2026 (with a follow-up to those who
    did not initially respond) and given the opportunity to answer all questions. Only the responses of candidates who answered the questions are
    included. None of the candidates' responses were modified in any way before
    being published on this resource page.</p>

    <p><u>For the <strong>August 2026 Primary Election and November 2026 General
    Election</strong></u>, only candidates in
    the following elections were contacted<sup>1</sup>:</p>

    <div>
      <div class="stance-race-flat">US Senate Special Election</div>
      <details class="stance-race-group">
        <summary>US House of Representatives</summary>
          <ul>
            <li>Districts 24, 27, and 28</li>
          </ul>
      </details>
      <div class="stance-race-flat">Florida Governor</div>
      <details class="stance-race-group">
        <summary>Florida State Senate</summary>
          <ul>
            <li>Districts 34, 36, 38, and 40</li>
          </ul>
      </details>
      <details class="stance-race-group">
        <summary>Florida State House of Representatives</summary>
          <ul>
            <li>Districts 106, 107, 108, 109, 110, 111, 112, 113, 114, 115, 116,
            117, 118, 119, and 120</li>
          </ul>
      </details>
    </div>
    <p><small><sup>1</sup> These primary elections were prioritized because
    they have more than one official candidate on the ballot.</small></p>

    <p>The contacted candidates include those running in both the August 2026
    primary election and the November 2026 general election.</p>
</StanceStatePage>
